 the   team   analysis   of   the   observations?   There   was   a   group   chat   to   reassure   the   objectives   of   the   interview,   the   vital   questions   and   the   approach   to   take   to   the   interviewee.   The   interview   was   conducted   by   one   member   of   the   group,   who   met   the   subject   at   work.   The   prepared   tone   was   a   relaxed   conversation,   trying   to   make   the   interviewee   comfortable   and   receptive   to   the   questions   and   bring   positive   insights   on   the   testing.   Some   days   after   the   interview,   there   was   a   group   meeting   to   check   the   results   and   discuss   the   obtained   results   and   give   360   feedback   to   understand   everyone’s   insights.     What   were   the   diﬃculties   you   faced   when   looking   for   interviewees?   And   What   do   you   think   would   help   when   trying   to   reach   5   interviewees?   I   would   have   loved   to   ﬁnd   a   subject   with   a   proﬁle   more   focused   on   the   basketball   administration   or   court   maintenance   industry,   nonetheless,   the   interviewee   as   an   athlete   gave   interesting   insights.   The   timing   for   this   activity   was   narrow   being   so   close   to   Christmas   Holidays,   it   would   have   been   easier   to   ﬁnd   more   meaningful   subjects   with   more   time   span.   We   even   tried   to   contact   optimal   proﬁles   online   but   for   the   same   reasons   and   their   agenda   I   guess,   couldn’t   get   done.   Years   ago   I   supported   this   kind   of   process   in   a   testing   lab,   in   my   last   job   as   an   IT   Leader,   and   I   understand   it   takes   a   lot   of   time   and   resources   to   get   valuable   outputs,   so   I   understand   a   little   bit   of   the   activity   and   with   the   limited   time   we   did   what   we   could.     What   are   the   most   suppressive   comments   from   the   interview?   The   interviewee   was   skeptical   of   the   durability   of   the   system   and   its   components.   Pointing   to   the   possibility   of   large   amounts   of   spills   and   how   they   could   be   resolved   by   the   surface   we   were   working   on.     Which   were   the   observations   that   generated   the   most   discussion   or   took   the   longest   time?   How   the   system   works,   taking   notice   of   the   tiny   holes   and   the   air   pumps   the   spill   onto   the   draining   properly.     It   is   a   long   shot   as   a   prototype   and   it   is   an   interesting   one   as   well,   the   interviewee   as   the   team   are   encouraged   on   the   opportunities   it   could   have   on   the   sport   and   help   on   health,   basketball   game   dynamics   and   business.     How   would   you   prepare   yourself   to   use   the   interview   technique   in   your   projects,   initiatives   or   jobs?   And,   what   you   consider   improving   for   obtaining   more   learning   from   the   interviews.   As   I   already   commented   on   the   second   question,   I’m   a   bit   aware   of   the   good   practices   on   this   kind   of   activities,   the   following   steps   should   be   contemplated:   ●   Get   the   right   personnel   like   UX   designers,   Quality   Analysts,   Business   Analysts,   Product   Owners,   Support   Analysts,   etc.   ●   Develop   a   well   thought   sprint   process   to   get   better   and   more   concise   results.   ●   Train   and   develop   better   practices   for   each   part   of   the   sprint   planning   and   how   each   step   is   important   to   get   optimal   outputs.   ●   Enjoy   the   process   and   prepare   physically   and   mentally   to   exhausting   meetings   😅 .\n\nPlease provide your response in valid JSON format:\n{\n    "analysis": "Your analysis here",\n    "criterion_scores": {\n        "criterion1": "score",\n        "criterion2": "score"\n    },\n    "total_score": "final_score",\n    "feedback": "Your feedback here"\n}\n\n\nAssistant:'}], 'model': 'claude-3-haiku-20240307', 'temperature': 0.0}}
