tmosphere. Prior to the meetings, we checked all equipment, including the camera, microphone, and internet connection. We provided the interviewees with a comprehensive agenda in advance, detailing introductions and an overview of our product, the grass-cutting robot Patch Play. Team roles were well established: Giacomo led the interview, Paolo documented notes, while the other team members observed. We also designated someone to oversee technical details to guarantee a smooth interview process. This distribution of tasks helped us concentrate on collecting and recording valuable insights. For the team analysis of observations, we held a collaborative in-person meeting, followed by online sessions to finalize the observation matrix. We organized feedback with shared documents, whiteboards, and digital boards, ensuring that all insights were categorized into actionable items sections. 2. Difficulties in Finding Interviewees: We faced minimal challenges in recruiting interviewees since they were professional connections made during past internships. Nonetheless, broadening the interview pool to five participants could have benefited from leveraging professional networks or attending industry-related events to find more candidates stakeholders. 3. Suppressive Comments from the Interviews:\xa0The most notable suppressive comments focused on key aspects of our product: Reliability: Issues regarding the robot’s reliability in prolonged use. Adaptability: The robot’s capacity to navigate various field conditions.  Training/Usability: User-friendliness for operators of different technical skill levels. Feedback on the storyboard focused on steps 3, 5, and 6, explicitly emphasising the clarity of processes, practicality, and evaluation metrics. 4. Observations That Generated the Most Discussion:\xa0Two primary observations sparked the most extended discussions during our analysis: Scalability of the Robot: Gino questioned whether the robot could handle more extensive or complex fields without performance issues. Long-Term Reliability and Maintenance: Oliver raised concerns about the robot’s durability and the ease of performing maintenance over time. These discussions led to deep dives into potential design adjustments and strategy refinements, ensuring the product’s alignment with real-world expectations. 5. Additional Considerations:\xa0The rapport and familiarity among team members improved our performance. A common understanding of objectives and open communication nurtured a collaborative and efficient atmosphere. Additionally, showcasing and discussing the storyboard during interviews offered beneficial visual aids, clarified ideas, and encouraged focused feedback. Conclusion:\xa0This interview process revealed key areas for improvement and emphasised the value of collaborative evaluation in enhancing our product. Future interviews might be strengthened by including a wider range of participants to capture diverse viewpoints and ensure thorough validation of the product features. Preparation for Future Interviews:\xa0To make the most of the interview technique in upcoming projects or roles, it’s vital to create ideal conditions for all participants. This involves choosing a suitable time and platform, formulating specific open-ended questions, and nurturing an engaging environment that promotes natural discussions. Additionally, employing tools for comprehensive analysis after the interview is essential for extracting actionable insights. Following up with interviewees to express thanks and offer feedback on the session is also a beneficial practice for sustaining professional relationships and fostering future collaboration. This outlines how I plan to apply the skills I\'ve gained throughout this process in my future interview endeavors.\n\nPlease provide your response in valid JSON format:\n{\n    "analysis": "Your analysis here",\n    "criterion_scores": {\n        "criterion1": "score",\n        "criterion2": "score"\n    },\n    "total_score": "final_score",\n    "feedback": "Your feedback here"\n}\n\n\nAssistant:'}], 'model': 'claude-3-haiku-20240307', 'temperature': 0.0}}
