ews </Category>  <Heuristics> 1. **10:** The argument incorporates at least 3 interviews. 2. **8-9:** The argument includes less o equal than 2 interviews. 3. **5-7:** The argument includes less or equal than 1 interviews. 4. **2-4:** There is no interviews identified. 5. **1:** There is a general approach to talking about interviews of any kind. 6. **0:** No interviews or evidence of such are provided. </Heuristics> <Category> Syntax </Category>  <Heuristics> 1. **10:** Sentence structure is varied and enhances the readability and engagement of the writing. No syntax errors are present. 2. **8-9:** Sentence structure is clear and varied but includes minor awkwardness or redundancy. 3. **6-7:** Sentence structure is functional but lacks variety or includes some awkward constructions. 4. **4-5:** Sentence structure is often repetitive or overly simplistic, reducing engagement and clarity. 5. **1-3:** Sentence structure is confusing or poorly constructed, with significant redundancy or awkwardness. 6. **0:** Sentence structure is entirely disorganized, making the writing unreadable. </Heuristics> Application of Use of Evidence Scoring Example: Score 0: No sources or real-world examples. Score 5: One credible interview is cited but no project referred (e.g., referencing user names nor application to the contexts). Score 10: Includes three interviews (e.g., interviewees names cited) for the projet, such as citing a project on sports related industries or entities. This detailed breakdown ensures consistency in scoring and facilitates improvement by identifying specific areas of weakness in an essay. Let me know if you need further clarifications or adjustments!`\n\nStudent\'s Solution:\nConsumer   Market   Research   Interview   Summary   Essay       Agentify   Sports   Agency     Group   Members:   Loukemy   Billard,   Sai-Rahul   Jajimogga,   Margaux   Veyne,   Julia   Castro   Lobo,   Isaias   Gutierrez   Gil,   Alejandra   Carmargo   and   Go-Molemo   Moloabi                 Author/W riter:   Go-Molemo   Moloabi              Inter views   regar ding   the   assessment   of   the   Agentify   platform   obtained   valuable   insights   from   our   exper t   inter view/consultation   with   Angel   Guar diola,   ESBS   Spor ts   Events   Lectur er/Pr ofessor ,   who   has   a   number   of   years   of   experience   in   the   spor ts   sponsorship   and   brand   collabor ation   business.   This   analysis   will   cover   four   main   topics   of   discussion:   how   the   inter view   envir onment   was   prepar ed   and   the   methodology   regar ding   the   analysis   of   the   team,   complications   related   to   ﬁnding   qualiﬁed   inter viewees,   the   feedback   with   the   highest   perceived   value,   and   the   obser vations   which   created   the   most   team   discussions.   This   structur ed   appr oach   allowed   us   to   identify   key   areas   that   needed   impr ovement   while   also   conﬁrming   some   aspects   of   our   design   and   functionality   of   the   platform.   The   inter view   with   Angel   Guar diola   was   structur ed   around   the   inter view   guidelines   provided,   which   ensur ed   consistency   and   focus   in   conducting   the   session.     In   using   Bubble.io   as   a   platform   for   development,   the   form   of   questioning   was   inﬂuenced,   especially   when   focusing   on   user   inter face   and   functionality   aspects.   The   obser vation   matrix   -   Agentify   Inter view   Sheet.xlsx .   Which   allowed   us   to   systematically   recor d   responses   across   key   areas   of   inter est,   such   as   brand   identity ,   user   experience,   and   technical   implementation.   The   following   detailed   examination   presents   our   ﬁndings   and   recommendations   based   on   this   exper t   inter view ,   which   has   proved   instrumental   in   shaping   the   futur e   development   of   the   Agentify   platform.         The   setting   of   the   inter view   was   prepar ed   on   Micr osoft   Teams,   as   the   base   platform   for   an   ideal   envir onment   concerning   remote   communication   and   recor ding.   Befor e   conducting   the   inter view   with   Angel   Guar diola,   the   team   agreed   upon   the   plan   for   documentation   and   prepar ed   structur ed   obser vation   templates   with   the   purpose   of   collecting   both   verbal   feedback   and   non-v erbal   signals.   A   joint   session   was   conducted   during   the   team   analysis   phase   wher e   members   shar ed   the   obser vations   systematically   taken   during   the   main   areas   of   focus:   brand   identity ,   user   experience,   and   strategic   areas.   This   helped   in   systematically   organizing   all   the   information   gather ed   from   the   exper t   inter view   regar ding   sponsorship   processes   and   functionality   of   the   platform   for   more   effectiv e   analysis.   The   biggest   challenge   in   securing   inter views   was   identifying   exper ts   who   could   compr ehensiv ely   provide   insight   into   sponsorship   and   brand   collabor ation   in   spor ts.   As   much   as   we   were   able   to   inter view   Angel   Guar diola,   ﬁnding   other   qualiﬁed   inter viewees   was   rather   challenging   due   to   their   limited   availability ,   shor tage   of   time,   and   the   specializ ed   natur e   of   our   platform \'s   focus.   While   explaining   and   trying   to   reach   the   target   of   ﬁve   inter viewees,   we   would   recommend   increasing   our   outreach   by:   using   our   network   with   brand   partners   such   as   El   Corte   Inglés;   reaching   out   to   spor ts   feder ations;   event   management   professionals;   using   professional   networks   in   the   spor ts   industr y.   This,   together   with   ﬂexibility   regar ding   scheduling   and   added   value   propositions   for   the   participation   of   exper ts,   would   secur e   more   exper t   inter views.     The   most   effectiv e   feedback   from   the   inter view   with   Angel   Guar diola   was   related   to   a   number   of   critical   aspects   that   need   serious   attention   on   the   platform.   First,   he   identiﬁed   the   proﬁle   section   as   highly   problematic,   requiring   too   much   information   upfront,   and   it   should   be   completely   redesigned   into   multiple   stages.   Another   striking   obser vation   was   the   lack   of   diversity   in   the   visual   content   on   the   platform;   this   needs   immediate   attention.   He   further   elabor ated   that   the   missing   key   elements   include   the   call-t o-action   buttons   and   direct   access   to   the   blogs   from   within   the   newsletter   section,   which   impede   the   degr ee   of   user   inter action.   This   comment   was   suppr essiv e   because   such   a   comment   pointed   towar d   fundamental   ﬂaws   in   the   design   of   the   platform,   which   could   hurt   its   core   use   and   adoption.     Extensiv e   discussion   and   analysis   time   was   made   based   on   three   critical   areas   of   the   site.   The   registr ation   process   involved   a   lot   of   discussion,   especially   about   the   amount   of   information   requir ed   and   how   it   should   be   reorganiz ed   into   steps.   The   newsletter   function   was   discussed   at   great   length   by   the   team,   who   debated   its   shor tcomings,   such   as   the   lack   of   direct   access   to   the   blog,   the   inability   to   attach   news   articles,   and   the   frequent   updating   of   content.   Consider able   discussion   time   was   spent   on   the   content   strategy   of   the   platform,   especially   on   how   variety   could   be   included   in   the   form   of   sponsorship   oppor tunities,   competition   coverage,   and   results   tracking.   Speciﬁcally ,   the   team   was   engr ossed   in   how   such   elements   would   be   integr ated   into   the   platform   while   keeping   the   inter face   clean   and   intuitiv e.       How   would   you   prepare   yourself   to   use   the   interview   technique   in   your   projects,   initiatives   or   jobs?   And,   what   do   you   consider   Improving   for   obtaining   more   learning   from   the   interviews?     To   arm   yourself   for   using   inter view   techniques   in   your   projects,   initiativ es,   or   jobs,   a   broad   appr oach   is   necessar y.   Do   some   deep   readings   of   both   the   subject   matter   and   the   persons   you   will   inter view .   Get   familiariz ed   with   structur ed,   semi-structur ed,   and   unstructur ed   appr oaches   to   inter viewing   to   pick   out   which   one   will   work   best   for   you.   Practice   activ e   listening   skills   and   construct   open-ended   questions   that   foster   lengthy   responses.   Further,   mak e   an   inter view   guide   of   topics   that   will   be   covered   and   some   possible   probes   for   complete   coverage.   In   addition,   the   skill   of   establishing   rappor t   in   a   shor t   time   will   help   in   getting   good   information.   You   may   also   conduct   mock   inter views   with   colleagues   or   friends   to   better   your   skills   and   instill   conﬁdence.     With   inter viewing,   this   usually   means   the   need   for   impr ovement   in   analytics   and   systematic   elabor ation   of   results   for   further   data   processing.   Right   after   each   inter view ,   try   to   sum   up   in   your   head   what   has   been   hear d   and   what   meanings   or   patterns   seem   to   emer ge   across   conv ersations.   Develop   an   excellent   note-taking   method   or   even   tape-r ecor d   inter views   if   a   respondent   does   not   object   to   preser ve   minute   details.   Impr ove   your   inter viewing   skills   over   time   by   reﬂecting   on   the   inter views   you   have   conducted,   soliciting   feedback   from   inter viewees   or   your   peers   wher e   appr opriate.   Keep   informed   about   new   inter view   methods   and   tools   that   may   be   helpful   in   collecting   and   analyzing   data.   In   this   way,   you   will   be   able   to   continually   impr ove   your   skills   and   be   more   effectiv e   at   gathering   valuable   information   from   inter views   and   applying   it   appr opriately   to   your   projects   or   initiativ es.       Documentation   and   Additional   Research/Information     Our   analysis   was   supplemented   by:   ●   Detailed   observation   matrices   documenting   user   interactions   ●   Technical   documentation   from   Bubble.io   implementation   ●   Comparative   analysis   of   similar   platforms   in   the   sports   sponsorship   space   ●   Integration   of   Design   Sprint   principles   in   the   evaluation   process   This   comprehensive   approach,   combining   technical   development   insights   with   user   experience   research,   has   provided   a   robust   foundation   for   future   platform   improvements   and   development   directions.     Roles   and   Responsibilities     Makers:   Loukemy   Billard   and   Go-Molemo   Moloabi   Stitchers:   Margaux   Veyne   and   Alejandra   Carmargo   Asset   Collector:   Collector:   Sai-Rahul   Jajimogga   Writer:   Julia   Castro   Lobo   Interviewer:   Isaias   Gutierrez   Gil     Makers:     Bubble   Apps:   https://agentify .bubbleapps.io/version-test/ai_landing_page_1       Stitchers   and   Asset   Collector   Work   https://www .canva.com/design/DAGccnfDe7c/4kioFg35l7gmz3a9tvxTBQ/edit?utm_c ontent=DAGccnfDe7c&utm_campaign=designshare&utm_medium=link2&utm_sourc e=sharebutton     